    "result_text": "All tests green. The full suite ran with exit code 0, and aggregating every surefire report shows **26 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence).\n\n**Core logic** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n- Added `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city`, prepended before `LAST3`.\n- Replaced the global `findAll().size() + 1` counter with a per-city count: it iterates `findAll()` and counts owners whose city matches (case-insensitively), then adds one. Since this step still runs before `SaveOwner` inside the write transaction, the new owner is excluded, so each created owner gets the next per-city number.\n\nEverything derived from `customerCode` is rebuilt automatically: `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` composes `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it now reads `SYD-SMI-0007-M26` off the new code with no logic change.\n\n**Documentation updated in lockstep** so the contract stays consistent:\n- `AssignCustomerCode` javadoc\n- `owners.POST.yml` step comment\n- `openapi.yml` `customerCode` description + example (`SYD-FRA-0007`) and `membershipNumber` example (`SYD-SMI-0007-M26`)\n- `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` javadoc example\n\nThe relevant checkpoints pass: Cp16 (regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`), Cp09 (two Sydney owners get `SYD-ALP-`/`SYD-BRA-` with consecutive per-city sequence numbers), Cp14 (membership number rebuilt on the new code), and Cp15 (membership tier, unaffected).",
